==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/mɔlç/|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
Alteration (''-ch'' due to {{term|Lurch|lang=de}}) of {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|mol|lang=gmh}}, {{term|molle|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|mol|lang=goh}}, {{term|mollo|mol(l)o|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*mulô}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*molh₂-o-}} (compare Lithuanian {{term|mulvas|mul̃vas|lang=lt}} ‘yellow, clayey’, Latin {{term|mulleus|lang=la}} ‘ruddy (shoes)’, Sanskrit {{term|mála}} ‘dirt’), from {{m|ine-pro|*melh₂-}} ‘dark color’.<ref>Wolfgang Pfeifer, ed., ''Etymologisches Wörterbuch des Deutschen'', s.v. “Molch” (Munich: Deutscher Taschenbucher Vertrag, 2005).</ref> More at {{l|de|malen}}.

